  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63697,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uterine corpus and cervix and within endometriosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63698,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The clinical features are related to the underlying etiology. Serum hCG is elevated in gestational cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63699,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are insufficient epidemiological data.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63700,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Arias-Stella reaction results from an increase or imbalance of hormones.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63701,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The extent of changes and degree of atypia are dependent on the levels of hormones, stage of pregnancy, and type and dosage of exogenous hormones.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63702,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63703,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is usually partial or near-complete involvement of glands, tufts, or papillae, in which the cells have abundant eosinophilic or glycogen-rich clear cytoplasm. Hobnail cells may be seen. The nuclei are highly atypical and the chromatin is either smudged or vesicular. Nuclear pseudoinclusions may be present. Mitotic figures are rare. Immunohistochemical stains have limited value, because many of them overlap with those of the differential diagnosis clear cell carcinoma {30608233; 27045514; 31094885}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63704,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63705,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63706,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 233,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> focal microscopic nature of atypical cells and absence of invasion; highly atypical columnar, cuboidal, or hobnail cells with abundant clear or eosinophilic cytoplasm; enlarged irregular nuclei with smudged or vesicular chromatin, or with pseudoinclusion; lack of mitoses; strong association with pregnancy or hormonal drugs.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
